From 26e4a7bccdde7fe81cfb5f6d5769693aba45b8ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aliosa27 <aliosa27@aliosa27.me>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:09:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/21] AT+SYSCFG and AT+SCAN? reply through atcmd_printf

syscfg_dump() now prints with atcmd_printf, so AT+SYSCFG output reaches
the web AT console and netAT, not only the UART log.

AT+SCAN? lists the last scan results (+SCAN:<bssid>,<MHz>,<signal>,
<enc>,<ssid>) then OK; AT+SCAN still only starts the scan. Also fix the
handler's ifidx type (uint8 made the "< 0" check dead).
---
 NOTES.md               |  2 +-
 project/syscfg.c       | 59 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------------
 sdk/lib/common/atcmd.c | 22 +++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md
index d0066d3..bea18da 100644
--- a/NOTES.md
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ So the DHCP change was not the (only) cause. **Leading theory: the image size.**
 
 ## AT reply gaps (found 2026-11-18, not fixed yet)
 
-The web AT console (and any AT client) waits for `OK`/`ERROR`, which only `atcmd_printf` output carries. `os_printf` output, including `atcmd_err()`, goes to the UART log only. Of the handlers in `sdk/lib/common/atcmd.c`, only `AT+SYSCFG` has been fixed: `atcmd_ok` after `syscfg_dump()`. The other 123 handlers are in the closed libs and were not audited. Still open, on the user's request:
+The web AT console (and any AT client) waits for `OK`/`ERROR`, which only `atcmd_printf` output carries. `os_printf` output, including `atcmd_err()`, goes to the UART log only. Of the handlers in `sdk/lib/common/atcmd.c`, only `AT+SYSCFG` has been fixed: `syscfg_dump()` (`project/syscfg.c`, called only from that handler) prints with `atcmd_printf`, and the handler ends with `atcmd_ok`. `AT+SCAN` only starts a background scan; `AT+SCAN?` (added) lists the last results as `+SCAN:<bssid>,<MHz>,<signal>,<enc 0|1>,<ssid>` lines, then `OK`. The other 123 handlers are in the closed libs and were not audited. Still open, on the user's request:
 
 - **No reply on the normal path:**
   - `AT+LOADDEF`: resets without `OK`; `AT+RST` sends `OK` first.
